      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:08 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2024-24-362",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ae8402906c3f6b8a66be948faae8f08b6932b93d4d98c8f81904d14e8c4aa7c7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ae8402906c3f-0000-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES: PATRICK M. JAICOMO, ESQUIRE, Arlington, Virginia; on behalf of the Petitioners. FREDERICK LIU, Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Respondents. CHRISTOPHER E. MILLS, ESQUIRE, Charleston, South Carolina; Court-appointed amicus curiae in support of the judgment below on Question 1."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Patrick M. Jaicomo",
      "case_id": "2024-24-362",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ae8402906c3f6b8a66be948faae8f08b6932b93d4d98c8f81904d14e8c4aa7c7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ae8402906c3f-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "Congress amended the Federal Tort Claims Act in 1974 to ensure a legal remedy for the intentional torts of federal police. The text of the law enforcement proviso is phrased affirmatively as a freestanding rule. With regard to acts or omissions of investigative or law enforcement officers of the United States Government, the FTCA shall apply to any claim arising out of six intentional torts. The United States is therefore liable for these intentional torts when committed by FBI agents empowered by law to execute searches, seizures, and arrests."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2024-24-362",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ae8402906c3f6b8a66be948faae8f08b6932b93d4d98c8f81904d14e8c4aa7c7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ae8402906c3f-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: How broadly does the proviso extend?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24-362",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ae8402906c3f6b8a66be948faae8f08b6932b93d4d98c8f81904d14e8c4aa7c7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ae8402906c3f-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Counsel, I don't think it was quite fair to say that everybody agrees on the first question. Amici doesn't agree on the first question."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2024-24-362",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ae8402906c3f6b8a66be948faae8f08b6932b93d4d98c8f81904d14e8c4aa7c7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ae8402906c3f-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "wouldn't ask the Court to get into the more\nenormously complicated aspects of the\ndiscretionary-function exception. Again, we're\nsimply saying there's a line where it's\nobviously not going to touch things like the law\nenforcement proviso."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2024-24-362",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ae8402906c3f6b8a66be948faae8f08b6932b93d4d98c8f81904d14e8c4aa7c7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ae8402906c3f-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "circuit. And so, if this Court is going to take\nthis issue up and provide any clarity, it should\nprovide clarity to all the circuits instead of\njust the Eleventh Circuit."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2024-24-362",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ae8402906c3f6b8a66be948faae8f08b6932b93d4d98c8f81904d14e8c4aa7c7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ae8402906c3f-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "Court need only decide the question about the proviso, namely, whether the proviso in subsection (h) modifies the discretionary-function exception in subsection (a).\nThe answer's no. Congress placed the proviso in subsection (h), and given that choice, the proviso modifies only subsection (h). It does not modify the discretionary-function exception in (a)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2024-24-362",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ae8402906c3f6b8a66be948faae8f08b6932b93d4d98c8f81904d14e8c4aa7c7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ae8402906c3f-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Do -- can a proviso such as this extend more broadly than -- than your -- than this case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24-362",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ae8402906c3f6b8a66be948faae8f08b6932b93d4d98c8f81904d14e8c4aa7c7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ae8402906c3f-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: So, counsel, what was Congress doing? It passed this proviso because of the Collinsville raids."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24-362",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ae8402906c3f6b8a66be948faae8f08b6932b93d4d98c8f81904d14e8c4aa7c7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ae8402906c3f-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: But why? Only because there was no warrant?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2024-24-362",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ae8402906c3f6b8a66be948faae8f08b6932b93d4d98c8f81904d14e8c4aa7c7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ae8402906c3f-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: No -- no policy says don't break down the wrong house, the door of a house?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2024-24-362",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ae8402906c3f6b8a66be948faae8f08b6932b93d4d98c8f81904d14e8c4aa7c7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ae8402906c3f-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: How about making sure you're on the right street? Is that -- is that --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2024-24-362",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ae8402906c3f6b8a66be948faae8f08b6932b93d4d98c8f81904d14e8c4aa7c7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ae8402906c3f-0001-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE JACKSON: But, I guess, Mr. Liu, the question is: How does that really differ from Colesville?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KAVANAUGH",
      "case_id": "2024-24-362",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ae8402906c3f6b8a66be948faae8f08b6932b93d4d98c8f81904d14e8c4aa7c7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ae8402906c3f-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "BUT, IF SO, THEY CAN SAY THAT?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Patrick M. Jaicomo",
      "case_id": "2024-24-362",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ae8402906c3f6b8a66be948faae8f08b6932b93d4d98c8f81904d14e8c4aa7c7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ae8402906c3f-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "THE FIRST THING I'D LIKE TO POINT OUT ALONG THE LINES OF WHAT JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR WAS ASKING IS THAT THE GOVERNMENT'S POSITION IN THIS CASE AND THE ELEVENTH CIRCUIT'S DECISION BELOW, THEIR UNDERSTANDING OF THE DISCRETIONARY-FUNCTION EXCEPTION WOULD DO TWO THINGS. ONE, IT WOULD EAT UP ALMOST ALL OF THE ENTIRE FTCA, BUT, TWO, MORE IMPORTANTLY, IT WOULD CERTAINLY EAT UP ALL THE CLAIMS THAT THE PROVISO WAS ENACTED TO PROVIDE LIABILITY FOR."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2024-24-362",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ae8402906c3f6b8a66be948faae8f08b6932b93d4d98c8f81904d14e8c4aa7c7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ae8402906c3f-0002-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "THE CASE IS SUBMITTED."
    },
